    "value": "Vert.x 5.0.0 introduces several modernizations and improvements to its stack, notably:\n\n- The API is now fully \"future\" based, dropping the old callback style across the stack.\n- It requires at least Java 11, modernizing the base technology.\n- The OpenAPI component (now named `vertx-openapi`) has been revised, aiming for better compatibility and a cleaner API with the OpenAPI 3.0 and 3.1 specs.\n- Its primary purpose remains to allow you to build web routers according to OpenAPI contracts, including request/response validation and parameter extraction. To use it in Vert.x 5.x, the Maven coordinates are:\n\n```xml\n\u003cdependency\u003e\n  \u003cgroupId\u003eio.vertx\u003c/groupId\u003e\n  \u003cartifactId\u003evertx-openapi\u003c/artifactId\u003e\n  \u003cversion\u003e5.1.2\u003c/version\u003e \u003c!-- Use the latest 5.x version available --\u003e\n\u003c/dependency\u003e\n```\n\nThe old artifact `vertx-web-openapi` or `vertx-web-openapi-router` is now refactored under `vertx-openapi`.\n\n**Sample Usage**:\nWith Vert.x 5.x, you use `OpenAPIContract` to load and validate your OpenAPI document, then navigate and attach handlers as needed. This can be done via:\n\n```java\nFuture\u003cOpenAPIContract\u003e contract = OpenAPIContract.from(vertx, \"your-openapi.yaml\");\n```\nYou then attach your route handlers according to OpenAPI `operationId`s.\n\n**Important**:\n- The OpenAPI library no longer downloads remote references automatically due to security.\n- Query/path parameters are always URL-decoded; header/cookie parameters can be controlled via a special extension.\n\n**Documentation and Release Notes**:\n- The new API brings more type-safety, future-based async handling, and makes it easier to create robust web APIs conforming tightly to OpenAPI specs【3:3†source】【3:8†source】【3:9†source】.\n\nFor more, visit the [official Vert.x OpenAPI documentation](https://vertx.io/docs/vertx-openapi/java/) and review the [Vert.x 5 changes on GitHub](https://