{"type":"output_text","text":{"value":"In Vert.x 5, `PgPoolOptions` is part of the Vert.x PostgreSQL client (`vertx-pg-client`). It is used to configure a connection pool to a PostgreSQL database. The class allows you to set options like host, port, database, user, password, maximum pool size, and other tuning settings.

Here’s a **basic example of how to use `PgPoolOptions` in Vert.x 5**:

```java
import io.vertx.pgclient.PgPool;
import io.vertx.pgclient.PgPoolOptions;
import io.vertx.sqlclient.PoolOptions;
import io.vertx.core.Vertx;

// Create Vert.x instance
Vertx vertx = Vertx.vertx();

// PgPoolOptions instance
PgPoolOptions options = new PgPoolOptions()
  .setHost("localhost")
  .setPort(5432)
  .setDatabase("mydb")
  .setUser("user")
  .setPassword("secret");

// Optionally configure the pool size
PoolOptions poolOptions = new PoolOptions().setMaxSize(5);

// Create the pool
PgPool client = PgPool.pool(vertx, options, poolOptions);
```

### Main configuration options in `PgPoolOptions`

- `.setHost(String)`: Set the server host.
- `.setPort(int)`: Set the server port.
- `.setDatabase(String)`: Set the database name.
- `.setUser(String)`: Set the username.
- `.setPassword(String)`: Set the password.
- `.setCachePreparedStatements(boolean)`: Enable/disable statement caching.
- `.setPipeliningLimit(int)`: Set the maximum number of pipelined requests.

You combine `PgPoolOptions` (connection details) **and** `PoolOptions` (pool sizing). This API is similar to Vert.x 4, but you should ensure you are using Vert.x 5 libraries in your project.

**Dependency (Maven example for Vert.x 5):**
```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>io.vertx</groupId>
  <artifactId>vertx-pg-client</artifactId>
  <version>5.x.x</version> <!-- Use the actual Vert.x 5 version -->
</dependency>
```

Check the [Vert.x 5 PostgreSQL client documentation](https://vertx.io/docs/vertx-pg-client/java/) for more advanced options and up-to-date details. If you’re migrating from Vert.x 4, most APIs remain compatible but review the changelog for breaking changes.","annotations":null},"bing_searches":null,"annotations":null}

