{"type":"output_text","text":{"value":"In Vert.x 5, the way to integrate Micrometer for metrics has evolved. You typically use `MicrometerMetricsOptions` to configure the metrics backend, such as Prometheus or InfluxDB. There used to be (in earlier versions and in some guides/examples) a method or pattern to programmatically "set" or inject a custom `MicrometerRegistry` (or MeterRegistry in Micrometer).

In Vert.x 5.x, you can still programmatically bind a custom Micrometer registry via `MicrometerMetricsOptions#setMicrometerRegistry(...)`. This is useful if:

- You already use a custom or shared MeterRegistry object elsewhere in your application.
- You want to use a backend or configuration not offered directly by Vert.x’ built-in SPI support.

Here’s how you could do this in code (Java example):

```java
import io.micrometer.core.instrument.MeterRegistry;
import io.micrometer.prometheus.PrometheusMeterRegistry;
import io.vertx.core.Vertx;
import io.vertx.micrometer.MicrometerMetricsOptions;

// Suppose you have your registry:
PrometheusMeterRegistry prometheusRegistry = new PrometheusMeterRegistry(PrometheusConfig.DEFAULT);

MicrometerMetricsOptions metricsOptions = new MicrometerMetricsOptions()
  .setMicrometerRegistry(prometheusRegistry)  // <-- This is the method!
  .setEnabled(true);

Vertx vertx = Vertx.vertx(new VertxOptions().setMetricsOptions(metricsOptions));
```

Make sure you have the right dependencies:
- `vertx-micrometer-metrics`
- The relevant Micrometer registry (`micrometer-registry-prometheus`, `micrometer-registry-influx`, etc.)

You can read more about `MicrometerMetricsOptions` and the `setMicrometerRegistry` method in the Vert.x Micrometer Metrics documentation and Javadocs. This setter is "mutually exclusive" with options for built-in backends (like `.setInfluxDbOptions()`), so set only the registry or the backend-specific options, not both at once【3:9†source】.

**References:**
- [Vert.x Micrometer Metrics documentation](https://github.com/vert-x3/vertx-micrometer-metrics)
- [MicrometerMetricsOptions in Vert.x](https://vertx.io/docs/vertx-micrometer-metrics/java/#custom_registry)

